# Data-Acquisition Node Design & Configuration Report

---

### 1. Architectural Plan & Analysis

#### Step 1: Clock Tree Synthesis (170 MHz SYSCLK / HCLK / PCLK1 / PCLK2)
* **Oscillator Source:** 12 MHz external crystal on HSE pins.
* **PLL Configuration:**
  * Target SYSCLK: 170 MHz.
  * Input division factor $M$: With $M = 3$, $f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} = 12\text{ MHz} / 3 = 4\text{ MHz}$, satisfying the PLL input clock specification ($2.66\text{ MHz} \le f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} \le 16\text{ MHz}$, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]).
  * Multiplier factor $N$: With $N = 85$, the VCO frequency is within Range 1 VCO limits ($96\text{ MHz} \le f_{\text{VCO}} \le 344\text{ MHz}$, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]).
  * Main PLL output division factor $R$: With $R = 2$, $f_{\text{SYSCLK}} = 170\text{ MHz}$ (0.0% error, max 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost Mode, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]).
  * Prescalers: AHB prescaler = 1 (HCLK = 170 MHz), APB1 prescaler = 1 (PCLK1 = 170 MHz), APB2 prescaler = 1 (PCLK2 = 170 MHz).
* **Core Voltage Scaling & Flash Latency:**
  * Operating at 170 MHz requires Range 1 Boost Mode. Clear `PWR_CR5.R1MODE` (bit 8 = 0) to enter Boost Mode ([STM32G474_RM0440 p.233, p.267]).
  * Flash latency in Range 1 Boost Mode at 170 MHz requires 4 wait states (`LATENCY = 4` WS, [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98]).

---

#### Step 2: Pin Allocation
* **I2C1 Bus:**
  * `PB8`: **I2C1_SCL** (AF4, open-drain, $5\text{ V}$-tolerant FT_f, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.74]).
  * `PB9`: **I2C1_SDA** (AF4, open-drain, $5\text{ V}$-tolerant FT_f, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.74]).
* **USART2 Link:**
  * `PA2`: **USART2_TX** (AF7, push-pull, high speed, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73]).
  * `PA3`: **USART2_RX** (AF7, input / pull-up, [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73]).

---

#### Step 3: Logic-Level Compatibility
* **STM32G474 (3.3 V) $\leftrightarrow$ ESP32-WROOM (3.3 V):**
  * STM32 output to ESP32 input:
    * High-level: $V_{\text{OH\_min}} = 2.9\text{ V} \ge V_{\text{IH\_min}} = 2.475\text{ V}$ (noise margin: $2.9\text{ V} - 2.475\text{ V} = 0.425\text{ V}$).
    * Low-level: $V_{\text{OL\_max}} = 0.4\text{ V} \le V_{\text{IL\_max}} = 0.825\text{ V}$ (noise margin: $0.825\text{ V} - 0.4\text{ V} = 0.425\text{ V}$).
    * Max voltage: $3.3\text{ V} \le 3.6\text{ V}$ max input.
  * ESP32 output to STM32 input:
    * High-level: $V_{\text{OH\_min}} = 2.64\text{ V} \ge V_{\text{IH\_min}} = 2.31\text{ V}$ (noise margin: $2.64\text{ V} - 2.31\text{ V} = 0.33\text{ V}$).
    * Low-level: $V_{\text{OL\_max}} = 0.33\text{ V} \le V_{\text{IL\_max}} = 0.99\text{ V}$ (noise margin: $0.99\text{ V} - 0.33\text{ V} = 0.66\text{ V}$).
    * Max voltage: $3.3\text{ V} \le 5.5\text{ V}$ max input on FT pins ([STM32G474_Datasheet p.82]).
  * Both links are directly logic-level compatible without shifters.
* **STM32G474 $\leftrightarrow$ Pressure Sensor Module (3.3 V I2C):**
  * Open-drain bus pulled to 3.3 V by $4.7\text{ k}\Omega$ pull-up resistors; PB8 and PB9 are 5 V-tolerant (`FT_f`), completely safe and compatible.

---

#### Step 4: Peripheral Register Configurations
* **USART2 (921600 Baud, 8N1):**
  * Clock source: PCLK1 = 170 MHz.
  * Oversampling by 16 (`OVER8 = 0`).
  * Divider: $\text{BRR} = 170000000 / 921600 = 184$.
  * Actual baud rate: $170000000 / 184 = 923913\text{ bps}$.
  * Baud rate error: $(923913 - 921600) / 921600 = +0.25\%$, well within the $\pm 2\%$ requirement.
* **I2C1 (Standard Mode 100 kHz):**
  * Peripheral clock: PCLK1 = 170 MHz.
  * Standard mode (100 kHz SCL) timing register configured for 170 MHz source:
    * Prescaler division: `PRESC = 15` ($t_{\text{PRESC}} = (15 + 1) / 170\text{ MHz} = 94.12\text{ ns}$).
    * `SCLH = 48`, `SCLL = 53`, `SDADEL = 2`, `SCLDEL = 4`.

---

#### Step 5: Power Budget & LDO Evaluation
* **Load Current on 3.3 V Rail:**
  * Digital Pressure Sensor Module: 1 mA (specified by user).
  * STM32G474: $\approx 40\text{ mA}$ typical in Run mode at 170 MHz.
  * ESP32-WROOM: Current in 802.11b transmit mode reaches 240 mA ([ESP32_Datasheet p.52]). Furthermore, the ESP32 datasheet explicitly states in Recommended Power Supply Characteristics (Table 5-2) that the current delivered by the external power supply must be at least 0.5 A (500 mA, [ESP32_Datasheet p.51]).
  * Combined continuous load during Wi-Fi transmission: $40\text{ mA} + 1\text{ mA} + 240\text{ mA} = 281\text{ mA}$.
* **Regulator Adequacy Check:**
  * The current load of 281 mA exceeds the LDO rating of 250 mA.
  * With RF calibration and peak Wi-Fi bursts requiring up to 500 mA, the 250 mA LDO will enter thermal shutdown or drop out of regulation, inducing brownouts.
  * **Verdict:** The 250 mA LDO is **inadequate**. A 3.3 V regulator rated for at least 500 mA (ideally 1 A) must be used.

---

### 2. Bare-Metal CMSIS Implementation

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

int main(void)
{
    /* =========================================================================
     * 1. CLOCK CONFIGURATION: HSE (12 MHz) -> PLL -> SYSCLK (170 MHz)
     * ========================================================================= */

    // Enable PWR clock on APB1
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    // Switch voltage regulator to Range 1 Boost Mode (clear R1MODE in PWR_CR5)
    // Necessary for operating SYSCLK above 150 MHz up to 170 MHz
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    // Enable HSE crystal oscillator (12 MHz)
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSEON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSERDY)) {
        // Wait until HSE is stable
    }

    // Configure Flash latency: 4 wait states required at 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost Mode
    // Also enable Prefetch, Instruction Cache, and Data Cache
    FLASH->ACR = (FLASH->ACR & ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_Msk) 
               | FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS 
               | FLASH_ACR_PRFTEN 
               | FLASH_ACR_ICEN 
               | FLASH_ACR_DCEN;

    // Configure PLL:
    // HSE = 12 MHz
    // PLLM = 3 (bits: 2) -> f_IN = 12 MHz / 3 = 4 MHz
    // PLLN = 85           -> f_VCO = 4 MHz * 85
    // PLLR = 2 (bits: 0)  -> f_SYSCLK = 170 MHz
    // PLLREN = 1          -> Enable PLLR output
    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSE
                 | (2U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos)
                 | (85U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos)
                 | RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    // Enable PLL
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY)) {
        // Wait until PLL is locked
    }

    // Set AHB, APB1, and APB2 prescalers to 1 (division factor 1)
    RCC->CFGR &= ~(RCC_CFGR_HPRE_Msk | RCC_CFGR_PPRE1_Msk | RCC_CFGR_PPRE2_Msk);

    // Switch system clock source to PLL
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_SW_Msk) | RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS_Msk) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL) {
        // Wait until PLL is used as system clock
    }

    /* =========================================================================
     * 2. GPIO PIN ALLOCATION AND CONFIGURATION
     * ========================================================================= */
    // Enable GPIOA and GPIOB clocks
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN | RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOBEN;

    /* --- Configure USART2 Pins: PA2 (TX) and PA3 (RX) --- */
    // Alternate Function AF7 (USART2)
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Msk);
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Pos); // AF mode (10b)

    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED2_Pos); // High speed for TX

    GPIOA->PUPDR &= ~(GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD2_Msk | GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD3_Msk);
    GPIOA->PUPDR |= (1U << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD3_Pos); // Pull-up on RX line

    GPIOA->AFR[0] &= ~(GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Msk | GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Msk);
    GPIOA->AFR[0] |= (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos); // AF7

    /* --- Configure I2C1 Pins: PB8 (SCL) and PB9 (SDA) --- */
    // Alternate Function AF4 (I2C1), Open-Drain
    GPIOB->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Msk);
    GPIOB->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Pos); // AF mode (10b)

    GPIOB->OTYPER |= GPIO_OTYPER_OT8 | GPIO_OTYPER_OT9; // Open-Drain

    GPIOB->PUPDR &= ~(GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD8_Msk | GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD9_Msk);
    GPIOB->PUPDR |= (1U << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD8_Pos) | (1U << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD9_Pos); // Pull-up enabled

    GPIOB->AFR[1] &= ~(GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Msk | GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Msk);
    GPIOB->AFR[1] |= (4U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (4U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos); // AF4

    /* =========================================================================
     * 3. USART2 CONFIGURATION (921600 Baud, 8N1)
     * ========================================================================= */
    // Enable USART2 clock (APB1)
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_USART2EN;

    // Clear control register before configuring
    USART2->CR1 = 0;

    // BRR = fCK / Baud = 170,000,000 / 921,600 = 184 -> Actual: 923913 Baud (+0.25% error)
    USART2->BRR = 184U;

    // 1 stop bit (CR2 STOP = 00b)
    USART2->CR2 = 0;

    // Enable Transmitter, Receiver, and USART2 peripheral
    USART2->CR1 = USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE | USART_CR1_UE;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 4. I2C1 CONFIGURATION (Standard Mode 100 kHz)
     * ========================================================================= */
    // Enable I2C1 clock (APB1)
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_I2C1EN;

    // Ensure I2C1 is disabled before configuring timing
    I2C1->CR1 &= ~I2C_CR1_PE;

    // Standard mode 100 kHz timing on 170 MHz PCLK1:
    // PRESC = 15, SCLDEL = 4, SDADEL = 2, SCLH = 48, SCLL = 53
    I2C1->TIMINGR = (15U << I2C_TIMINGR_PRESC_Pos)
                  | (4U  << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLDEL_Pos)
                  | (2U  << I2C_TIMINGR_SDADEL_Pos)
                  | (48U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLH_Pos)
                  | (53U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLL_Pos);

    // Enable I2C1 peripheral
    I2C1->CR1 |= I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 5. MAIN ACQUISITION LOOP
     * ========================================================================= */
    while (1) {
        // Application data polling and forwarding loop
    }

    return 0;
}
